            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0573" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg488"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/994a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of the
                        Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Glass</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I take the liberty of
                    calling to your particular attention the negotiations now pending regarding
                    financial assistance to Liberia. As this is a matter to which we attach very
                    considerable importance and as the negotiations appear to grow somewhat
                    protracted, I should greatly appreciate if they could be carried through with
                    the greatest possible speed.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
